For $M = 6$: valid $d \in \{1, 2\}$, giving $Q_1 = 6$ (count $= 9$) and $Q_2 = 1$ (count $= 1$), total $= 10$. Brute-force checking all $(m,n)$ with $2^m-1, 2^n-1 \mid 63$ confirms exactly 10 valid pairs. ✓

